@OlaDevBoa Thanks for checking. The only red check on f87c87e is E2E, with a single failing test: `virtualization.spec.ts` › "contains horizontal trackpad gestures after focus leaves the grid" (`Expected: > 120, Received: 120`). This PR only touches the CSV export plugin and its unit test, and the same failure is intermittent without this change: with `npx playwright test e2e/virtualization.spec.ts -g 'horizontal trackpad' --repeat-each=20`, it failed 6 of 20 times on `main` (9f8762e) and 3 of 10 on this branch, with the same assertion.

So a re-run of the E2E job should get past it, although it can fail again. Unit tests and the SonarCloud quality gate show as passed on this commit; if you meant a different gate, could you point me to it? A separate PR to stabilize that test can follow if that helps.

This comment was drafted with Claude Code.
